# Where a proposal goes — the issue, not the documentation

**A design proposal is a comment on the issue it is for** (the forge is
GitHub for now), or in the discussion chat. Not a page in `docs/`: do not
pollute the knowledge graph with SDLC churn. A proposal published as a page
that later moves breaks every link to it.

## Why it is wrong beyond taste

The rendered site is the folio's **published output** and the knowledge graph
is what tools read. A design proposal is neither:

- it is an **argument about what to build**, superseded the moment it is
  decided
- its audience is one or two people, for about a week
- as a page it gets a **permanent URL**, so it is cited long after it stopped
  being true
- it goes through translation, QA sidecars and link auditing — all of which
  cost something, and none of which it needs

An issue comment has the right lifetime, the right audience and the right
tooling, and it sits next to the decision it produced.

## The test

> **Would somebody who does not work on this platform want to read it?**

If no, it is not documentation. A folio's reader wants to know what the
content says and how to work with it; they do not want to know which of four
options the platform chose for its work-plan store.

## Where each thing goes

| what | where |
|---|---|
| a design proposal, an options analysis, an impact assessment | a **comment on the issue** |
| a decision worth citing later | the issue, and one or two lines in the **skill** the decision governs |
| structured content worth keeping but not publishing | **`fsh-guts/`** — see [`fsh-guts`](../../../skills/kg/kg-core/fsh-guts.md) |
| how an agent should behave | a **skill**, per `AGENTS.md`'s own banner |
| what a reader of the folio needs | **`docs/`** |

## The exception

**Not everything in a proposal is churn.** The **argument** is churn and
belongs on the issue; the **rule that came out of it** is durable and belongs
in the skill it governs, in a paragraph. Treating all of a proposal as churn
gets this rule ignored the first time it is inconvenient.

So the move is not "delete the thinking". It is: put the conclusion where it
is enforced, put the argument where it is discussed, and keep the long form in
`fsh-guts/` if it is worth keeping at all.

